# HORO Shopify Admin Seeder — Environment Variables
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Option A — Static token (Custom App, recommended)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Create a Shopify custom app in your store:
#    Settings → Apps and sales channels → Develop apps → Create an app
# 2. Configure Admin API access scopes:
#    - read_metaobject_definitions
#    - write_metaobject_definitions
#    - read_metaobjects
#    - write_metaobjects
#    - read_products
#    - write_products
# 3. Install the app on your store and reveal the Admin API access token.
# 4. Copy this file to .env and paste the token.
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Option B — OAuth (Partner App)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# If you can't create a Custom App (e.g., development store redirects
# to Partner Dashboard), use your Partner app credentials instead.
# The script will open a browser for OAuth authorization.
# Set SHOPIFY_CLIENT_ID and SHOPIFY_CLIENT_SECRET from your
# Partner Dashboard → App → API credentials.

SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN=horo-9109.myshopify.com
SHOPIFY_API_VERSION=2026-01

# Option A: Static token (uncomment and fill)
# SHOPIFY_ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN=shpat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Option B: OAuth (uncomment and fill with Partner app credentials)
SHOPIFY_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
SHOPIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret_here
# SHOPIFY_SCOPES=read_metaobject_definitions,write_metaobject_definitions,read_metaobjects,write_metaobjects,read_products,write_products
